{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up","id":44641,"title":"What happens if a Virgin Goddess, well.....gives it up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-07T20:49:02-08:00","id":44641,"title":"What happens if a Virgin Goddess, well.....gives it up?","content":"I started a thread similar to this one back on the old forum. But I seem to recall that at that time, we were pretty much at our nadir in terms of people stopping by, so it didn't become much of a discussion. Thought I'd try again here.<br /> <br /> For the record? I'm not trying to be crude or disrespectful here. I would like this to be a serious discussion. Jokes are okay, but I think this is a fairly important topic that could be significant somewhere down the road.<br /> <br /> The topic also came back to my mind tonight when I conversed with my player who is playing a Scion of Ishtar. We were working on his Health relic: a set of Babylonian beard decorations, which also gives him a once-a-day Super Seduction power. During our conversation, my friend jokingly said &quot;Yeah, with that thing, I should be able to nail Athena!&quot;<br /> <br /> Typical caveman laughter ensued.<br /> <br /> But after the laughter was over, I began to contemplate the question once again. Now my player may be joking about trying to seduce Athena in our game, but what if he isn't? What if he really does try? More importantly? What happens if he SUCEEDS?<br /> <br /> Really, let's expand the discussion here. What do you think happens in ANY scenario in which a virgin goddess breaks her chastity? Does Fate punish her? Does Fate punish the man with whom she does the deed? Both of them? Or is it just a change of status for the goddess in question? Nothing really comes from Fate. The goddess simply isn't a virgin anymore.<br /> <br /> Obviously, being a virgin goddess is tied quite heavily into said goddess's Legend. It seems likely that there may be SOME ramifications from Fate for breaking with a Fatebound Role. Or is it such a big deal? In the case of both Artemis and Athena, their oaths of eternal virginity were their own choice. Is it possible that Fate might just decide that the oath was theirs to make and theirs to break? If Athena, one day, legitimately falls in love with a man and wants to be with him physically, can she? Or would Fate stop her? If she does it, what happens?<br /> <br /> For that matter, I know there are a few virgin goddesses in other mythologies, but I'm not too familiar with them. Are they ALL like Artemis and Athena, or are there some variations on the theme?<br /> <br /> For that matter, does choice factor in to this thing? In the above example, my friend mentioned the idea of using a Super Seduction power that would basically FORCE Athena to go to bed with him. These days, we call that rape. For that matter, rape is a real possibility in the Scion setting. I mean there's a war going on. What might happen if Athena were to be defeated in battle by some Titanspawn and he decided to take full advantage of his victory?<br /> <br /> There are other ways in which a virgin goddess could be forced into surrendering her chastity. I recall at least one Greek myth where a couple giants were threatening Olympus and demanded that the Gods hand over Hera and Artemis to them. The Gods pretended to comply, but Artemis tricked them into killing each other. Well, what were to happen if a similar situation presented itself and virgin goddess had no choice but to surrender? It doesn't even need to be a force thing. What if some Trickster god managed to trap a virgin goddess into some kind of wager with her virginity as the prize? If he wins? What then?<br /> <br /> So that's the question. What might happen if a virgin goddess willingly gives up her chastity? What if it's taken from her by force or trickery? What kind of backlash might come from Fate? If any? What other concerns might there be? Obviously, the social and/or political ramifications are easy enough to guess. Zeus, would obviously be pissed at ANYONE who deflowered his favorite daughter. What other ramifications might there be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:32:47-08:00","id":44663,"title":"","content":"I think that the likelihood or a virgin goddess willingly giving up her virginity is very slim. It's part of who she is and is part of her legend and has been for thousands of years. It's intrinsic to her nature by now to resist the advances of men.<br /> <br /> However, this is Scion, so fuck all that. This is the game of slim-chance things happening. Zeus overthrew Kronos, why can't your Scions overthrow Zeus? Or deflower Artemis, as the case may be.<br /> <br /> I don't think there would be Fate ramifications. You're forging a new legend by doing this. You're the god who deflowered the virgin goddess! And then Zeus got pissed and tried to fry your ass with a thunderbolt so you killed him. Or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:51:02-08:00","id":44673,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be interesting if Fate actually have ramifications for this, at least if the Virgin Gods and Godesses were deflowered by force the union would result in the most foul beast that ever was---perhaps everything about it would be a direct antithesis to the being that robbed the virginity. Or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:57:14-08:00","id":44677,"title":"","content":"Having such a massive change in your Legend may well actually result in a drop to your Legend until/unless you can &quot;fix&quot; things or resolve the crisis. If Athena lost her virginity, she'd lose a big chunk of what makes her <i>Athena</i>. It would be very distressing not just to her, psychologically, but also to Fate itself. So, yeah, hellacious results all around.<br /> <br /> Aside from possibly losing Legend (permanent Legend!) for having such a central part of your character taken away, Fatebindings may also get involved. <i>How </i>exactly depends on how you run Fatebonding. The RAW system doesn't have much in the way of teeth, so it'd be fairly useless. Different systems might impose a penalty on the goddess involved (I am unaware of any adult <i>male</i> virgin deities) until she does something to rectify the situation. Maybe she avenges her loss by murdering the crap out of whoever deflowered her, or she arranges for them to be emasculated, or something. Or she marries them and establishes a new pattern in her Legend. Legends can change.<br /> <br /> If the loss of virginity is consensual, think about <i>why</i> it's done. Think also about <i>why</i> the virginity of that goddess mattered. What did it represent? Was it there to show she was not an adult woman? Was it there to make her independent, free from marriage and servitude to a husband? In at least one version of Greek mythology, Artemis's big thing wasn't that she hated the idea of having sex, it was she hated the idea of <i>being a wife</i>. She made Zeus promise never to make her get <i>married</i>. In a modern world where virginity isn't tied to marriage nearly so much, might Artemis loosen up and decide that as long as she can still be a strong, asswhuppin, independent woman, who cares if she gets jiggy with it? Then you have to think how <i>that</i> affects her Legend. <br /> <br /> In general, I would say that if the goddess rolls with the change in her Legend and either embraces it (willing loss) or sets about somehow avenging her loss (unwilling loss) then she's worked that event into her Legend and she doesn't particularly suffer penalties for it. If she spends time freaking out (understandable) and is unable to resolve the situation, then she's probably going to lose Legend until she finds a way to bind her identity back together. That's basically what Gods are, after all. Their entire being is based on their conceptual identity. Artemis losing her virginity would be like Heracles losing his superhuman strength, or Ares becoming a pacifist. A really more accurate comparison might be what would happen if Hephaestus cured his lameness, since that's closer to the same kind of conditional vs vocational thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You touched on something that pretty much every Scion group is gunna have to deal with: Epic Socials make free will and informed choice a <i>very</i> shaky subject. What possible definition of free will and consensual sex includes one party having Epic Appearance 5? How could any mortal <i>at all</i> ever turn that down? If Aphrodite walks up to a happily married father and tells him to have sex with her, <i>he does that right then.</i> It doesn't matter that he loves his wife, that he would never hurt her or want to betray her. Aphrodite's Epic Socials blow <i>waaay</i> past what he's capable of dealing with and so he does whatever she wants, no possible resistance at all. Is that in any way <i>not</i> rape? Really, past a 2-3 Legend point difference, the issue is the same. There's no real way to beat someone with an Epic Social that's significantly stronger than your resist stat (whatever that may be in your game). They own you, if they want you. They can convince you it was your idea, or make you want them, or just be <i>so sexy</i> that you can't possibly turn them down... but none of that is your free choice because you are so far out of your league there was never a question of you putting up any resistance at all. Not to mention the innate level of coercion going on in any LegendaryBeing-mortal relationship where the mortal is aware of what the Legendary being is. If you turn down the Morrigan for sex, she's probably going to kill you somehow. Painfully. Horribly. <br /> <br /> So, that right there, is a big deal. And of course rape happens <i>all the time</i> in mythology. It's everywhere. All over the place, in every ancient culture. Just buttloads of it. Zeus &quot;ravishes&quot; women constantly, his brothers both do it. Morrigan is out there with her sex-or-death 'seductions' and Tlazlteotl is just waiting for you to fail to resist her so she can murder you for your sins. Gods tend to be terrible people and even the ones that don't set <i>out</i> to be specifically terrible are hugely egocentric and may not be able to possibly understand why someone would not want to have sex with them. Does Thor understand why someone <i>wouldn't</i> want to try his hammer on for size? No. Because he's Thor and obviously anyone he wants would also want him. Avoiding the unwanted advances of a God generally doesn't end well. You get turned into landscape features, or monsters, or you have to flee to the ends of the earth. <br /> <br /> <br /> End result? If you have <i>any</i> PC's that have expressed interest in Epic Socials and <i>especially</i> Epic Appearance, you need to have a talk with your entire group. It is going to be a situation that arises eventually. Even if your Epically Sexy PC doesn't want to seduce people, they're Epically Sexy. People will want to seduce <i>them</i>. It's gunna happen. You need to be sure everyone in your group is on the same page. I cannot stress enough how incredibly important it is to do that. I've had issues where players said they were alright with something, then later it turned out they were not at all alright with it and had just been trying to avoid making a fuss. That's not good. Do everything you can to make sure your entire group is comfortable with what's happening at your table. Obviously if someone says they're fine and really isn't, that's not a situation you can deal with easily. All you can do is try to be open and make it plain that you're trying your best to accommodate everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:24:48-08:00","id":44689,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm off to bed, so I'll talk more about this tomorrow.<br /> <br /> But Telgar? As far as having &quot;the talk&quot; with my group? We've all been friends for many years. We've been through many games together, from Old World of Darkness Vampire, to New World Vampire, to Scion, to Exalted. We know how the game is played and how creepy the Social powers are. I'm not really worried on that particular front.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, it's never bad advice to check and make sure everyone's on the same page. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:57:18-08:00","id":44707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=44677#post44677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A really more accurate comparison might be what would happen if Hephaestus cured his lameness, since that's closer to the same kind of conditional vs vocational thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cyber-Hephaestus! Half god, half robot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T23:02:48-08:00","id":44715,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's very slim. Like really REALLY drunk and unconscious kind of slim. Still, there are ways that virgin goddesses can give birth and still be a virgin. Take Athena for example. In the Percy Jackson books, Athena MENTALLY gave birth to Annabeth. She literally thought about her and she came to be. I would think that virgin deities have divine ways to produce like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T23:06:46-08:00","id":44720,"title":"","content":"I will note that at my own table, Artemis' &quot;virginity&quot; was a matter of Ancient Greeks not having a diverse enough vocabulary. She forswore &quot;the touch of man&quot;.... she said absolutely nothing about women and nymphs.<br /> <br /> And as a goddess of female health and the reproductive cycle, she is more than capable of impregnating her lovers should she choose to.<br /> <br /> <br /> The same does not apply to Hestia (who is celibate as a matter of 'purity' as the myths and the religion of her cult implies - rejecting whatever desires she may have; and given that virgin purity is so central to her Legend, beaking that oath would likely reduce her to near mortal status... and which point she'd bury herself alive as sacrifice to herself like so many lapsed [or raped] Vestal Virgins), or Athena (who is on the ace-spectrum and uninterested in sex - her children are cooked up in her lab/loom, or adopted half-siblings because Zeus has so many extra - unlike Hestia, virginity is not central to her purview, so she would not be nearly so affected by sex, but she is uninterested none the less, and no more likely to take any lover than Artemis is a male one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-08-2014, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T01:41:33-08:00","id":44768,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's something intensely personal to the Goddess in question. There are a number of myths in which Athena or Hestia are propositioned by various Gods, or certain Gods attempt to rape them. A lot is made of the fact that these attempts never succeed. Hestia would probably be most strongly affected, since being a virgin IS the greatest part of her Legend. By contrast, Athena has a lot more going for her.<br /> <br /> Consider also what a culture would consider virginity. The Greeks did not consider lesbian intercourse as sex, and so any of these Goddesses who had sex with a woman (forced or not) would probably still count as a virgin in the eyes of her Legend (hell, she probably still counts herself as a virgin. There's enough nudge nudge, wink wink in Greek narrative to assume that Artemis follows this mindset).<br /> <br /> By contrast, consider Guan Yin. She is a virgin Goddess, but unlike the Greek trio, this fact has no relevance to her mythology. It's not a gigantic part of her image, and is really more a side-effect of her being a Buddhist nun than a feature unto itself. She would never abandon her duties for love, and even if she was raped (in which case your player character is an evil, evil man), I doubt the powers of Fate would come down on HER. They would come down on the person who just raped a nun, because that is some epically bad karma (and seriously, Guan Yin is like the nicest God ever, so don't do it).<br /> <br /> As for virgin Goddesses in other myths, I am not an expert, but here are my thoughts on the ones I know.<br /> <br /> The Yazata Goddesses Ard and Anahita are virgin goddesses, but I do not know if them losing it would impact them heavily since I'm not sure how large a factor it is in their legends. Ard's brother Sraosha would probably gut you like a pig for touching his little sister though.<br /> <br /> When the Aztec virgin Goddess Quetzalpetlatl was raped by her brother Quetzalcoatl in a drunken stupor, he had to immolate himself in penance, and she disappears off the face of mythology. So one suspects that losing the one thing that defined her Legend, she ceased to exist. Hestia isn't that bad off, but she should consider this a rather scary idea.<br /> <br /> Finally, there is Sarasvati, who holds the rather unique position of being both married, and explicitly a virgin Goddess. Her virginity is a symbol of her association with the Arts and Sciences, higher, intellectual forms of expression and enquiry. The loss of her virginity (also likely to be forced, since she's shown no signs of straying from Brahma for ages) is likely to heavily diminish her power over these areas, while leaving her Water powers as a river Goddess untouched. The rapist should consider also the fact that Shiva and Sarasvati have a strong friendship in Hindu myth, so he's definitely going to have both Shiva and Kali on his tail. I would not wish to be this person.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, the Canaanite Goddess Anat is sometimes called a virgin, and at other times is Ba'al's lover. She's never both. If you do choose to run her as a virgin, and if a player gets the idea of raping her in his head, I would suggest you ask him to create a new character since Anat is likely to tear him apart and eat his entrails. This is the Goddess who killed Death himself while he was in the Underworld. It would be a sobering reminder as to why certain Goddesses remain virgins unless they want to).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T06:48:15-08:00","id":44871,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Most Goddesses started out as virgins.<br /> Just look at Persephone. Was Hades punished for her rape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:00:32-08:00","id":44909,"title":"","content":"Wow, this has turned into a real quality discussion. Much better than the last time I brought this up.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it seems like it's more about how the goddess in question might deal with the change that matters the most. So it's really more a question of &quot;What are the circumstances under which it happens, and how does the goddess respond?&quot;<br /> <br /> @Telgar: I like your idea that it's how the goddess deals with the situation that matters. Especially the idea of the goddess avenging her violation. So, given my scenario of Athena being defeated and raped on the battlefield, if she later tracked down that Titanspawn and killed him, the only thing that really changes for her is that she's no longer a virgin goddess, but she'd retain everything else in her Legend? The idea of a virgin goddess mitigating her losses through marriage is also interesting. Especially interesting if the shoe ends up being on the other foot, and the goddess basically FORCES her ravisher into the marriage in some way. &quot;You had your fun, now you're gonna make an honest goddess out of me.....or else.&quot; Sounds epic.<br /> <br /> @glamourweaver: Yes, my group tends to agree with you that Artemis, in particular, is not so much a &quot;virgin goddess&quot; as she is a &quot;lesbian goddess.&quot; As Samudra pointed out, the Greeks simply didn't consider girl-on-girl sex to BE sex in the first place. So no force or magical trickery required if a FEMALE Scion ends up having sex with Artemis, and definitely no backlash from Fate.<br /> <br /> @Samudra: Great stuff in that post. I really learned a lot. Totally agree with you about Guan Yin, as well. If any of MY players ever raped her, I'd kill the living SHIT out of his character. As far as Ard and Anahita? I had heard that Anahita was a virgin, but I didn't know about Ard. Strangely, though, I recall that Anahita is like simultaneously a virgin goddess and a mother figure. Is that more of a symbolic thing, or is there something else at work? Sarasvati is a fascinating case, and I really need to put some more time into researching her.<br /> <br /> @Shadowflame: The difference there is that we don't have any evidence that Persephone had sworn to remain a virgin. Her mother was extremely protective of her, which would make it difficult at best for her to actually have sex, but there's no proof that there was any kind of Fatebound oath involved. That's kinda the defining quality of a &quot;virgin goddess&quot; is that she has CHOSEN to remain a virgin. Simply not having had the opportunity to engage in sex is not the same thing as declaring to Fate itself that one would NEVER seek the pleasures of the flesh.<br /> <br /> I also found myself remembering that Aphrodite, at least, has a habit of routinely restoring her virginity through a ritual bathing. I think even Hera does it from time to time. I wonder if a deflowered virgin goddess would have the same option? Could a virgin goddess restore her virgin status through some means?<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of virgin goddesses having Scions. Okay, according to the RAW, all virgin goddesses pretty much just adopt. However, as JackalopeVegas and glamourweaver have pointed out, there are OTHER means by which virgin goddesses might produce offspring without the need for sex. Anyone else have any other examples of this?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:01:26-08:00","id":44911,"title":"","content":"I don't think anything breaks. I think Athena would only have daughters (and as a fertility goddess she can certainly decide for herself).<br /> <br /> But you then have to decide if Athena saved her virginity for your Scion, or if she's actually been mattress-hopping for a while and her legend just hasn't caught up. One is a seriously &quot;d'awww&quot; sort of thing and the other is turning established mythology on its head, which makes for a good icebreaker on the whole concept of sacrosanctness (and its distinct absence) of existing legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:41:34-08:00","id":44930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=44909#post44909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Samudra: Great stuff in that post. I really learned a lot. Totally agree with you about Guan Yin, as well. If any of MY players ever raped her, I'd kill the living SHIT out of his character. As far as Ard and Anahita? I had heard that Anahita was a virgin, but I didn't know about Ard. Strangely, though, I recall that Anahita is like simultaneously a virgin goddess and a mother figure. Is that more of a symbolic thing, or is there something else at work? Sarasvati is a fascinating case, and I really need to put some more time into researching her.<br /> <br /> I also found myself remembering that Aphrodite, at least, has a habit of routinely restoring her virginity through a ritual bathing. I think even Hera does it from time to time. I wonder if a deflowered virgin goddess would have the same option? Could a virgin goddess restore her virgin status through some means?<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of virgin goddesses having Scions. Okay, according to the RAW, all virgin goddesses pretty much just adopt. However, as JackalopeVegas and glamourweaver have pointed out, there are OTHER means by which virgin goddesses might produce offspring without the need for sex. Anyone else have any other examples of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Anahita, well, Anahita is the mistress of all the waters of the world. She purifies the rains to make them potable. She feeds the crops that feed the World. Perhaps most importantly, she provides the clarity of mind to see through the Lies of Ahriman. Thus Anahita is Spiritual Mother to all mankind. But she's never physically had children.<br /> <br /> You have that myth backwards. Hera is the one who renews her virginity once a year. The idea of Aphrodite becoming a virgin would be as unwelcome to Fate as the idea of Hestia being deflowered. As such, I don't Aphrodite has ever even considered regaining her virginity.<br /> <br /> He's not a virgin Goddess, obviously, but all of Brahma's children are manasputras/manaskanyas (lit. sons/daughters of the mind in Sanskrit). Brahma creates them from pure thought, so you have mythological precedence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:32:39-08:00","id":44944,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. I could've sworn I read about Aphrodite having done the &quot;Virginity Restoration&quot; thing at least once. Ah, well. My memory sucks sometimes.<br /> <br /> So, okay, so Anahita is a mother figure in the sense of being a provider and protector of mankind. Like any good mother. That does lead me to wonder whether her virgin status is merely due to the fact that she simply hasn't found a prospective husband yet. I believe I read that the Yazata consider marriage an absolutely sacred institution. They're not nearly as tolerant of promiscuity as the Theoi are. They're not quite as extreme about it as, say, the Teotl. They don't mind you enjoying sex. But they'd prefer to see you legally married before you indulge. (Unless I'm totally off my rocker again.) So, it could be more that Anahita doesn't indulge in sex because she hasn't found a husband yet. Rather than out of some belief that her virginity is a sacred thing that must never be forsaken.<br /> <br /> So, Scions formed from the mind of their divine parents are an option? Interesting. Filing that one away for possible use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:48:18-08:00","id":44954,"title":"","content":"There are some traditions that hold that Anahita is married to Mithra, but others that don't, so it will be an ST call. I'm pretty certain JSR runs them as husband and wife. She's still always a virgin though. So...I suppose I spoke too soon when I said Sarasvati was a unique case. Actually, come to think of it: Sarasvati and Anahita are both Water Goddesses who are considered Mother Figures while remaining virgins, all while still being married, and both have associations with the clarity of thought! Holy Shit, they could be twins! (Though I would not advise you to say this in either's presence. You'll probably find out pretty quickly what it means to drown on dry land). Yet another example of the fascinating relationship between the Yazata and Deva.<br /> <br /> Since you're using JSR's rules, I'd say that both the Avatars of both the Health Purview and the Artistry Purview could be used to create a Scion out of thin air. I'd assume the latter is how Brahma does it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T10:09:01-08:00","id":44964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=44954#post44954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some traditions that hold that Anahita is married to Mithra, but others that don't, so it will be an ST call. I'm pretty certain JSR runs them as husband and wife. She's still always a virgin though. So...I suppose I spoke too soon when I said Sarasvati was a unique case. Actually, come to think of it: Sarasvati and Anahita are both Water Goddesses who are considered Mother Figures while remaining virgins, all while still being married, and both have associations with the clarity of thought! Holy Shit, they could be twins! (Though I would not advise you to say this in either's presence. You'll probably find out pretty quickly what it means to drown on dry land). Yet another example of the fascinating relationship between the Yazata and Deva.<br /> <br /> Since you're using JSR's rules, I'd say that both the Avatars of both the Health Purview and the Artistry Purview could be used to create a Scion out of thin air. I'd assume the latter is how Brahma does it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That IS an interesting parallel between the Yazata and the Deva. Weird how stuff like that happens.<br /> <br /> As far as creating Scions through the Healt or Artistry Avatars? Funny story? John and Anne just talked about that on their latest, or second latest vlog. They are actually of the opinion that the Creator can't really create a full-fledged Scion, even with a sample of human blood on hand. Their opinion was that Scions are special and need that spark of real Humanity in order to be what they are. They theorize that the Creator can create a God or a CLONE of a Scion, but not a whole-new whole-cloth Scion. Not sure if I agree completely, but they laid out a pretty good argument that I don't currently feel qualified to refute.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, if they're right? Then I'm not sure how Scion would deal with the whole &quot;Dreaming Scions into being&quot; approach. Maybe just a unique power of some sort? Or maybe Brahma (or Athena) uses some very elaborate combination of Epic Intelligence, Health, and Artistry to weave everything together. Like Epic Intelligence to determine how it's done, over to Health to make the raw materials, and Artistry to finish the refining process? That'd be my best guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T16:36:51-08:00","id":45213,"title":"","content":"My general ruling has been if the goddess is a virgin, and has been thing long, it will take Ultimates to get you in the sack with her. With caveats.<br /> <br /> Greek Virginity hinges on sex with a man, so many Dodekatheon goddesses, like Artimis or Athena, are romancable by a woman with high Epic Socials. Very high in Athena's case (Epic Int helps a lot too, just in general), merely significant with good play with Artemis, though growing...extra equipment for kidmaking with Epic Appearance powers is out of the question. The vast majority of Scion characters have been bisexual with a handful of straight ones over time, so not an issue.<br /> <br /> Epona is not considered virginal in Scion, so that problem gets a pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T16:47:40-08:00","id":45217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45213#post45213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general ruling has been if the goddess is a virgin, and has been thing long, it will take Ultimates to get you in the sack with her. With caveats.<br /> <br /> Greek Virginity hinges on sex with a man, so many Dodekatheon goddesses, like Artimis or Athena, are romancable by a woman with high Epic Socials. Very high in Athena's case (Epic Int helps a lot too, just in general), merely significant with good play with Artemis, though growing...extra equipment for kidmaking with Epic Appearance powers is out of the question. The vast majority of Scion characters have been bisexual with a handful of straight ones over time, so not an issue.<br /> <br /> Epona is not considered virginal in Scion, so that problem gets a pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds about right if you're looking to accomplish the deed consensually. With Athena, you probably definitely need Epic Intelligence in addition to Appearance and/or Charisma. You have to charm her AND fascinate her with your intellect. Artemis? Sounds about right as well. She's a little more earthy, so just being charming and good-looking as possible and showing her respect could make it at least possible. But yeah, Epics may be required as well.<br /> <br /> My only information about Epona comes from JSR and they say that she's a virgin. Are you referring to the official Nemetondevos file that was only released in France? What more information is there about Epona and the other Nemetondevos? Again, my only intel on them comes from JSR, and sadly it isn't that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T16:55:02-08:00","id":45222,"title":"","content":"Could always try seduction through a dream...It's amazing how such a technique could have so much power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:00:22-08:00","id":45225,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45222#post45222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could always try seduction through a dream...It's amazing how such a technique could have so much power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also true.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, in JSR, the Illusion Purview has two Boons that allow you to enter a person's dreams and influence them. An intriguing thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:00:30-08:00","id":45226,"title":"","content":"I am referring to the Nemetondevos file, that is what we are using for European Celtic gods. Epona's virginity seems not totally settled on, but the Celts of Europe we know so damn little about. Being an unmarried and young goddess, as well as &quot;wild&quot; like Diana, the Romans seemed inclined to have her as a virgin goddess, but I don't really buy that the Celts really saw her that way.<br /> <br /> This is even ignoring the idea her partners were horses and her Scions come from those unions (though if a PC Scion of Epona ever does not identify their dad I am totally doing that. It would be hilarious especially for an E Strength/Stamina character).<br /> <br /> Pretty much any of my groups I have been in have people who would be unhappy with rapist PCs in the party, so non consensual is not so much an issue.<br /> <br /> No one has tried romancing virgin goddesses yet, I assume Artemis would like an athletic outdoorsy type with cunning, Athena would want someone well read and value Charisma over Appearance, and Hestia would like a more stereotypically masculine woman to &quot;have her cake and eat it too&quot; as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:22:40-08:00","id":45239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45226#post45226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am referring to the Nemetondevos file, that is what we are using for European Celtic gods. Epona's virginity seems not totally settled on, but the Celts of Europe we know so damn little about. Being an unmarried and young goddess, as well as &quot;wild&quot; like Diana, the Romans seemed inclined to have her as a virgin goddess, but I don't really buy that the Celts really saw her that way.<br /> <br /> This is even ignoring the idea her partners were horses and her Scions come from those unions (though if a PC Scion of Epona ever does not identify their dad I am totally doing that. It would be hilarious especially for an E Strength/Stamina character).<br /> <br /> Pretty much any of my groups I have been in have people who would be unhappy with rapist PCs in the party, so non consensual is not so much an issue.<br /> <br /> No one has tried romancing virgin goddesses yet, I assume Artemis would like an athletic outdoorsy type with cunning, Athena would want someone well read and value Charisma over Appearance, and Hestia would like a more stereotypically masculine woman to &quot;have her cake and eat it too&quot; as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never been able to get the translated version of the Nemetondevos file. Thus, I'm dependent on JSR's information (which is great, thankfully) for all my Gaulish needs.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I don't think the Gauls were big on virginity so I doubt the virgin thing is for real with Epona. It makes sense that the Romans would see her that way. After all, in their world view, it was the natural state of a woman to be married to a man. Thus, a goddess without a husband must be either a &quot;slut&quot; or a virgin goddess. They probably chose to call her a virgin goddess, since &quot;virginity&quot; is kind of associated with being invincible, and since they made her the patron goddess of their cavalry, it makes sense they'd want her to have an air of invulnerability about her.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I don't think any of my players are interested in playing rapists. At least not in this game. Some of us are willing to go kinda dark, but we're well aware of each other's boundaries. No, if a virgin goddess gets forcibly deflowered in one of my games, it'll likely be an NPC that did the deed as part of some larger storyline. Now this particular situation with my player MAY go a little darker than we normally do. I will definitely talk things over with everybody before I'll approve anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:31:19-08:00","id":45242,"title":"","content":"Ah, I hope I did not have anything accusatory sounding there. I did not intend to.<br /> <br /> In general, I try to find out from players what their limits are. Rape and anything involving sex and kids tends to be off the table in most games. Some players have specific things they additionally don't want to deal with, we always try to know (one player does not like any stories involving people dying from ODing on drugs for personal reasons, for example, so no game with them in it has it come up, while others might).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:37:22-08:00","id":45247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45242#post45242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I hope I did not have anything accusatory sounding there. I did not intend to.<br /> <br /> In general, I try to find out from players what their limits are. Rape and anything involving sex and kids tends to be off the table in most games. Some players have specific things they additionally don't want to deal with, we always try to know (one player does not like any stories involving people dying from ODing on drugs for personal reasons, for example, so no game with them in it has it come up, while others might).</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I knew you weren't making accusations. But since rape is a common part of mythology, it's not a topic that I feel can be completely ignored, especially in a thread like this where we're talking about the different ways sex happens in Mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:40:47-08:00","id":45249,"title":"","content":"Oh yea, ignoring it and having PCs doing it (or being victims of it) are different things tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:41:53-08:00","id":45250,"title":"","content":"Yes, exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:49:12-08:00","id":45252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=44964#post44964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, if they're right? Then I'm not sure how Scion would deal with the whole &quot;Dreaming Scions into being&quot; approach. Maybe just a unique power of some sort? Or maybe Brahma (or Athena) uses some very elaborate combination of Epic Intelligence, Health, and Artistry to weave everything together. Like Epic Intelligence to determine how it's done, over to Health to make the raw materials, and Artistry to finish the refining process? That'd be my best guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deal with it like the Virgin Mary: all of a sudden, a mortal woman becomes impregnated by the power of the divine, without any sex being involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:51:44-08:00","id":45254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45252#post45252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deal with it like the Virgin Mary: all of a sudden, a mortal woman becomes impregnated by the power of the divine, without any sex being involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saaay. That's a pretty good idea, really. Yeah, immaculate conception might just work. There's no Health Boon right now that allows for spontaneous impregnation, but the more I think about it, the more I think there probably should be one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T18:08:03-08:00","id":45259,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it with Savior/Scourge, and that would be appropriately high power. If you wanted something lower level I would make it at least 9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T20:59:14-08:00","id":45359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45226#post45226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am referring to the Nemetondevos file, that is what we are using for European Celtic gods. Epona's virginity seems not totally settled on, but the Celts of Europe we know so damn little about. Being an unmarried and young goddess, as well as &quot;wild&quot; like Diana, the Romans seemed inclined to have her as a virgin goddess, but I don't really buy that the Celts really saw her that way.<br /> <br /> This is even ignoring the idea her partners were horses and her Scions come from those unions (though if a PC Scion of Epona ever does not identify their dad I am totally doing that. It would be hilarious especially for an E Strength/Stamina character).<br /> <br /> Pretty much any of my groups I have been in have people who would be unhappy with rapist PCs in the party, so non consensual is not so much an issue.<br /> <br /> No one has tried romancing virgin goddesses yet, I assume Artemis would like an athletic outdoorsy type with cunning, Athena would want someone well read and value Charisma over Appearance, and Hestia would like a more stereotypically masculine woman to &quot;have her cake and eat it too&quot; as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting to note that I don't think they would give a flying fuck about your attributes. They would be more interested in your accomplishments. Because those are what make you interesting.<br /> <br /> Artemis would like an outdoorsy sort...who told her stories of hunting Nemean lions on safari in Montenegro. Bonus points if they're true.<br /> <br /> Athena would probably be into someone who had written a particularly interesting book, written a gripping play, or designed an impressive structure (from an engineering standpoint).<br /> <br /> Hestia would probably be the toughest of the three to please and also the easiest. She probably goes for successful politicians or general contractors, both things Scions aren't super likely to be.<br /> <br /> As far as Epona, I'm not sure virginity was a concept that concerned Celts. It certainly held little appeal for the Norse, although Gefjun picked up some Greco-Roman virgin gloss, the historical Gefjun was supposedly married to Skjoldr, who is a legendary king of Denmark. He makes a cameo in <i>Beowulf.</i> He has, I quote, &quot;many sons.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:02:14-08:00","id":45360,"title":"","content":"Telgar wrote an interesting Stamina Knack a while back.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Unmatched Virility / Fertility</span></span></b><br /> Dice pool: None.<br /> Cost: None or 1 point of Legend.<br /> Prerequisites: Controlled Potency.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">This Knack represents total control of the Scion\u2019s reproductive abilities. They can determine the gender of any children they sire or bear at no cost. Further, they do not even need to engage in sexual intercourse with a prospective partner to create a child. Simply physical contact and the expenditure of one Legend point is enough for a Scion to cause pregnancy in their partner, or themselves. Such immaculate conceptions ignore normal gender limits, allowing a female Scion with this Knack to impregnate another woman without difficulty. Barring extensive use of the Health Purview, males cannot be made to bear children, even with this Knack.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:07:19-08:00","id":45365,"title":"","content":"Several things. First, the Virgin Goddess in question probably have relics and or fates making sure they <i>stay</i> virgins. Not to mention that their pantheons are probably going to gang up on whichever PC decides it's a good idea to convince a goddess that she needs to stop being a virgin and sleep with him for whatever reason (no, sexy auras aren't good enough reasons). I want to say the Greeks connected Athena's virginity to Athens' state of being protected so she'd probably not be willing to lose that for anything less than True Love(tm).<br /> <br /> But yeah, biggest issue is going to be pantheons that are suddenly wondering why you're sniffing around their goddesses. You don't have to just deal with Artemis, you have Apollo AND Zeus who'd probably get really furious at someone violating his daughter, a daughter he promised will never have to marry (and remember in the Bronze Age Greek households, folks, women who were raped or y'know, not-virgins usually were sold off to the rapists or to the guy who slept with her because damaged property values!). Athena's probably got Zeus backing her up because she's Athena and probably 110% asexual; and Hestia... well ... what sort of brother wants to see a punk-ass guy deflower his sister just because he's got a fancy bit of epic appearance and a relic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 01-09-2014, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T02:43:12-08:00","id":45464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45359#post45359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to note that I don't think they would give a flying fuck about your attributes. They would be more interested in your accomplishments. Because those are what make you interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attributes seemed pretty important to the Dodekatheon, especially appearance. They were among the pantheons who seemed MOST fixated on that, actually. I won't say accomplishments were not important, but attributes would be. After all, they are very human in their thoughts and attributes are pretty important to people.<br /> <br /> If we were talking about, say, Aesir or Pesedjet then I'd say accomplishments would be more important. But the Dodekatheon are...somewhat petty and superficial a lot of the time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T02:56:33-08:00","id":45467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45365#post45365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several things. First, the Virgin Goddess in question probably have relics and or fates making sure they <i>stay</i> virgins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Aynie. I was wondering when someone would bring up Divine IUDs and Chastity belts. Actually, I'm pretty sure there is a power involved entirely on killing or overcharging a given person's sex drive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention that their pantheons are probably going to gang up on whichever PC decides it's a good idea to convince a goddess that she needs to stop being a virgin and sleep with him for whatever reason (no, sexy auras aren't good enough reasons). </div> </div> </div>The obvious solution, is to seduce the entire pantheon. We do not do these things because they are easy, but because I am hard.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://moe.animecharactersdatabase.com/uploads/chars/4755-1392662722.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T08:36:46-08:00","id":45624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45467#post45467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious solution, is to seduce the entire pantheon. We do not do these things because they are easy, but because I am hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the only reasonable way you are going to be able to sleep with a virgin goddess is after a long campaign of social and political maneuvering. You would literally have to combine great deeds while constantly exposing the gods in the virgin's pantheon to your social powers for a prolonged period of time to make sure that it becomes safe for you to take action. The most reasonable way to do so is to approach it from the True Love(tm) angle.<br /> <br /> Otherwise that goddess is doing to report you with her sanctify band AND perception gods are going to notice what you are doing AND vigil brand is going to sound the alarm to any guardian gods. The response could be as &quot;tame&quot; as suddenly having to start dodging/soaking ricochet symphony arrows from thousands of miles away, to as &quot;extreme&quot; as a large number of gods and their retinue showing up with come running/rainbow bridge to deal with you. And they are not going to be amused at your presumption to sleep with their relative / distract them from the titan war / distract them from their favorite hobby.<br /> <br /> Even if the goddess in question is on the battlefield and about to be defeated by a Titan, someone is going to probably show up to save her from that fate at the cost of a military loss somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 01-09-2014, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T09:25:30-08:00","id":45657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45467#post45467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious solution, is to seduce the entire pantheon. We do not do these things because they are easy, but because I am hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>That comment made my day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T16:19:39-08:00","id":45901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45624#post45624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the only reasonable way you are going to be able to sleep with a virgin goddess is after a long campaign of social and political maneuvering. You would literally have to combine great deeds while constantly exposing the gods in the virgin's pantheon to your social powers for a prolonged period of time to make sure that it becomes safe for you to take action. The most reasonable way to do so is to approach it from the True Love(tm) angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can just be badass enough to seduce her anyway, like <a href=\"http://www.badassoftheweek.com/diomedes.html\" target=\"_blank\">Diomedes</a> and Athena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:28:05-08:00","id":45936,"title":"","content":"One person may be the one doing the deed, but make no mistake-screwing a god whose virginity is part of their identity is a full band task, with everyone else having to do some really heavy work to ensure the two have enough time alone for anything.<br /> <br /> Hope your friends are on board with this.<br /> <br /> ...I almost want to play this game now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:55:35-08:00","id":45947,"title":"","content":"I kinda think that the whole pantheon would have to respect her choice (assuming that). And if that were the case, then the pantheon would likely have an added god to their ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:47:46-08:00","id":45983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/44641-what-happens-if-a-virgin-goddess-well-gives-it-up?p=45901#post45901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can just be badass enough to seduce her anyway, like <a href=\"http://www.badassoftheweek.com/diomedes.html\" target=\"_blank\">Diomedes</a> and Athena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Athena was certainly proud of him, and he was certainly an amazingly impressive hero, but I do not think their relationship would be considered a seduction by any means. Athena has a long history of picking champions to represent her, Diomedes was simply the most badass of them all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T21:12:43-08:00","id":46041,"title":"","content":"Okay, so the common theory about Athena's virginity is that the Athenians started that story. The idea was that if their patron goddess was an eternal virgin, it would convey a certain invincibility to their city. Just as Athena has never been ravished, so Athens could never be ravished.<br /> <br /> ......Only Athens WAS ravished. More than once, in fact. Hell, the Persians flat-out SACKED it not long after Thermopylae.<br /> <br /> In Scion terms, what do you think this means? If the Athenians Fatebound Athena's virginity with the Fate of their own city, then how, exactly did Athens fall? When the Persians sacked Athens, did that mean that one of the Yazatas may have gotten one over on Athena? Or was the Fatebinding never really a thing and Athena simply advised the Athenians to allow Athens to be sacked as part of the larger war effort against the Persians?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T16:20:56-07:00","id":865177,"title":"","content":"I think the ramifications for it would depend on the context in which it happens. So far as I'm aware, there's nothing strictly forbidding Athena from having sex, she just doesn't seem interested in it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now Artemis, on the other hand, is seen as the protector of virgins and her legend revolves around fighting off the unwanted advances of men. <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>IF</b></span> your character manages to force themselves on her, you're pretty much destroying the very thing that she stands for, a guardian against rape. Of course, she's also kind of a blood thirsty maniac and is not going down without a fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are some other deities in mythology who can't have sex for other reasons. For example, many of them are castrated and simply don't possess a sex drive. Osiris doesn't have a penis anymore, which makes it physically impossible for him to have sex.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to reiterate, it shouldn't have any negative repercussions for seducing a virgin goddess unless their Legend provides a specific reason for why they have to remain virgins.<br /> <br /> <br /> On an additional note, I disagree with the idea that using epic Socials constitutes as rape. You're not dropping narcotics into their food and sleeping with them when they're out of their minds, you're persuading them through personality and charisma. If social skills and beauty constituted as rape than every celebrity in America should be found guilty for abusing the millions of fans that lust after them.<br /> <br /> Sure, your ability to seduce and persuade others may be supernaturally strong, but at the end of it all, it's still persuasion and seduction. Nobody tied down your partner and forced them to have sex with you, they went along with it of their own volition. If they regret what they did later, that's their own fault.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind Control, however, is a completely different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-13-2016, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}